{"id":812,"slug":"jericho","title":"Jericho","year":1937,"country":"United Kingdom","duration":75,"spine":null,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/812-jericho","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/d0606bfda6ec74c0019bd85bbe973ae0/6DSu10XLoj9GjtPJZGAxaXPs113oQD_large.jpg","description":"Seeking out new avenues for his artistry, Paul Robeson moved his family to London in 1928. During the next twelve years, he headlined six British films, pioneering uncharted territory for black actors and reaching a level of prominence unthinkable in Hollywood. Robeson's first British production, Zoltán Korda's Sanders of the River, however, ended up being an embarrassment for the actor, its story of an African tribal leader transformed into a celebration of the British Empire. As a result, Robeson sought more artistic control, eventually achieving it with Jericho, which features Robeson in what turned out to be his most satisfying film role, as a World War I officer who escapes his fate as a black man by fleeing to Africa and creating a new world for himself.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Thornton Freeland","slug":"thornton-freeland"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Paul Robeson","role":"\"Jericho\" Jackson","slug":"paul-robeson"},{"actor":"Henry Wilcoxon","role":"Captain Mack","slug":"henry-wilcoxon"},{"actor":"Wallace Ford","role":"Mike Clancy","slug":"wallace-ford"},{"actor":"Princess Kouka","role":"Gara","slug":"princess-kouka"},{"actor":"John Laurie","role":"Hassan","slug":"john-laurie"},{"actor":"James Carew","role":"Major Barnes","slug":"james-carew"},{"actor":"Lawrence Brown","role":"Private Face","slug":"lawrence-brown"},{"actor":"Rufus Fennell","role":"Sergeant Gamey","slug":"rufus-fennell"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Thornton Freeland","slug":"thornton-freeland"},{"role":"Producer","person":"Walter Futter","slug":null},{"role":"Adaptation by","person":"Robert N. Lee","slug":null},{"role":"Adaptation by","person":"Peter Ruric","sl